      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Semi-metallic brake pads are a bit like a heavy, slow-moving brick of a different kind, while ceramic pads are more like a nimble, light-footed creature that can dart away from danger. When you talk about heat dissipation, the semi-metallic pads act like a thick, warm blanket that absorbs a lot of the thermal energy, holding onto it for a long time. They are very efficient at soaking up the heat generated during those high-speed deceleration tests, but they can get so hot that the heat doesn't leave as quickly as you'd like. It's like a room full of a bunch of sleepy, hot goblins who are just sitting there, radiating warmth, making it hard for the air to circulate and cool things down.\n\nCeramic pads, on the other hand, are much more like a group of tiny, fast-moving goblins who are constantly hopping around, scattering the heat in every direction. They don't hold onto the thermal soak as tightly; instead, they allow the heat to dissipate much faster, keeping the rotor temperature spikes from building up into dangerous levels. If you think of the rotor as a giant oven, the semi-metallic pads are like a heavy pot that takes",
